{"name":"Brass Buttons","hex":"#dfac4c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic alloy of copper and zinc used in many industrial and plumbing applications.","A memorial or sepulchral tablet usually made of brass or latten: a monumental brass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of brass, of or pertaining to brass.","Of the color of brass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brass"},{"term":"buttons","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of button"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dung of sheep.","A remote control."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buttons"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotula coronopifolia","blocks":[{"text":"Cotula coronopifolia is a species of flowering plant in the aster family (Asteraceae). Commonly known as brass buttons, golden buttons, and buttonweed, it is native to southern Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cotula_coronopifolia_Sturm37.jpg/330px-Cotula_coronopifolia_Sturm37.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotula_coronopifolia"},{"title":"A Brass Button","blocks":[{"text":"A Brass Button is a 1911 American social drama film in one reel, released on February 1, 1911. It was produced by Reliance Film Company. The actors are James Kirkwood and probably Marion Leonard."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Brass_Button"},{"title":"Brass Buttons","blocks":[{"text":"Brass Buttons is a 1919 American silent comedy Western film directed by Henry King, and starring William Russell, Eileen Percy, and Helen Howard. A New York cop in Arizona tackles a gang of criminals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Brass_Buttons_%281919%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/330px-Brass_Buttons_%281919%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brass_Buttons"},{"title":"Brass","blocks":[{"text":"Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc, in proportions which can be varied to achieve different colours and mechanical, electrical, acoustic, and chemical properties, but copper typically has the larger proportion, generally 2⁄3 copper and 1⁄3 zinc. In use since prehistoric times, it is a substitutional alloy: atoms of the two constituents may replace each other within the same crystal structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg/330px-Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brass"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg/250px-Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg/500px-Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg/250px-Cotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACotula_coronopifolia_108269598.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg/330px-Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg/960px-Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg/330px-Cotula_coronopifolia_2.jpg?utm_sou